<<~ ahu #/contract>>

''The outcome bound.'' A verb's durable outcome rests in the daemon bag, syncs to every vessel and never shrinks, so `writeOutcome` bounds it. Any top-level array of the handler's result past `AUDIT_ARRAY_CAP` rows (32) rides as a summary in place of its rows: the row count, a tally per `decision` over the rows that carry one, a hash of the whole array, a sample of three, and every row whose decision reads `refuse` or `conflict`, whole, up to the cap (`held`), beside the count of such rows the summary leaves unnamed (`heldMore`). An array at or under the cap rides whole.

''A row a person must act on stays named.'' A refusal nobody can find stays unfixable, so a summary never counts a refusal it does not name without saying so: zero in `heldMore` states that `held` names every one. An array whose rows carry no decision (a LOAD's titles) tallies nothing, so no tally invents a decision nobody made.

''The reader asks again.'' The co-located CLI reads this same outcome as its answer. A caller that reads `heldMore` above zero, or a tally that proves less than it needs, asks again in waves under the cap, where every row rides whole; the ingest gesture pages so (`packages/lares-cli/src/ingest-core.ts`, `settleIngest`), prints each refused carrier with its refusal, and ends the run non-zero. A tripped mass-delete brake applies nothing, answers no carrier row, and ends the run non-zero under its own name; a carrier no answer accounts for ends it non-zero too. The watcher keeps what it still owes by address (each carrier that did not land, each deletion that did not apply), clears a debt only where a wave proves that address settled, and ends non-zero where any debt stands at its stop.

''A rename re-homes records that stand.'' A vanished source that holds no live record leaves nothing to re-home, so the island answers the arriving carrier as a plain ingest and the source as a tombstone that removes nothing (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/action-handler.ts`).

Witnesses: `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/verb-vm.test.ts` · `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/rename-rehomes-standing-records.test.ts` · `packages/lares-cli/tests/ingest-settles-every-row.test.ts`.

